 Hard vs Soft Constraints Hard constraint (via trajectory): traj_hard = NamedTrajectory(
    (x = randn(2, N), u = randn(1, N), Δt = fill(0.1, N));
    timestep = :Δt,
    controls = :u,
    final = (x = x_goal,),  # Exact constraint
) N = 50, (x = 1:2, u = 3:3, → Δt = 4:4) Soft constraint (via terminal objective): traj_soft = NamedTrajectory(
    (x = randn(2, N), u = randn(1, N), Δt = fill(0.1, N));
    timestep = :Δt,
    controls = :u,
    goal = (x = x_goal,),  # For reference only
)
obj_soft = TerminalObjective(x -> 100.0 * norm(x - x_goal)^2, :x, traj_soft) KnotPointObjective on [:x] at t = [50] Large weight approximates hard constraint

